# Keep the working copy byte-identical to what CI checks out. core.autocrlf gives a Windows working
# copy CRLF while the Linux runner checks out LF, so Spotless and Prettier, which read the working
# copy, fail locally on files that pass in CI, and any tool that rewrites a file with LF shows every
# line of it as changed. Pinning the ending here makes every clone agree, whatever its settings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The exception Gradle's own generated attributes make: cmd.exe misreads a batch file's labels and
# goto targets when its lines end in LF, so gradlew.bat keeps CRLF in every working copy.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.jar binary
